  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Ohio's 15th Congressional District election pits Republican incumbent Mike Carey against Democratic nominee Don Leonard and Libertarian candidate Brennan Barrington. The district covers Columbus suburbs and parts of western and central Ohio, including Pickaway, Madison, Fayette, Highland, and Miami counties. Ohio redrew its congressional map in October 2025 ahead of this election. Cook Political Report rates this race as 'Solid Republican,' though the redrawn map and Leonard's grassroots campaign have generated some Democratic interest. Carey, a former coal lobbyist first elected in a 2021 special election, emphasizes energy independence and conservative values, while Leonard, a former Ohio State professor, campaigns on economic fairness and healthcare access.",
