      "name": "Mike Carey",
      "party": "Republican",
      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Mike Carey (born March 13, 1971) is the incumbent U.S. Representative for Ohio's 15th Congressional District, first elected in a 2021 special election. He previously served as vice president of government affairs for American Consolidated Natural Resources, a coal company, and chaired the Ohio Coal Association. In Congress, he serves on the Ways and Means, House Administration, and Budget Committees, and has focused on energy policy, tax reform, and civility in government.",
