      "name": "Don Leonard",
      "party": "Democratic",
      "incumbent": false,
      "summary": "Don Leonard is the Democratic nominee for Ohio's 15th Congressional District. A former assistant professor of practice at Ohio State University's Knowlton School of Architecture, he holds a Ph.D. in Government from Cornell University and served as a Peace Corps volunteer in Bolivia. He defeated former state Representative Adam Miller in the May 5, 2026 Democratic primary, and campaigns as a 'Do Something Democrat' focused on economic fairness, affordable healthcare, housing, and childcare.",
